==Remaining Getting Around Changes==
The final round of changes from the <u>[https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/a=13/getting-around?oldschool=1 Getting Around Poll]</u> are here! You can see the batches we've previously released from this <u>[https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/a=13/holy-moleys-and-the-hooded-slayer-helm-are-here?oldschool=1 here]</u>, <u>[https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/a=13/deadman-annihilation-tweaks-shellbane-gryphon-cas--more?oldschool=1 here]</u>, <u>[https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/a=13/cow-boss-is-out-today?oldschool=1 here]</u> and <u>[https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/a=13/more-from-the-getting-around-poll?oldschool=1 here]</u>.

Before getting into the remaining changes from the poll, let's kick things off with a tweak for the Perfected Quetzal (i)...

===Tweaking How the Perfected Quetzal Whistle Becomes Infinite===
To start with, we're giving the Perfected Quetzal Whistle the same functionality as the Corrupted Bow of Faerdhinen. This means you can now work toward unlocking infinite charges gradually, rather than sticking with Hunter Rumours for extended periods before getting the most out of your whistle. Starting with this game update, charging any Quetzal Whistle will now contribute to the infinite unlock, counting toward the total requirement of 10,000 teleport charges worth of Hunter meat.

You can check your progress towards the unlock by asking about the Perfected Quetzal (i) to Soar Leader Pitri and giving him some hunter meat.

[[File:Remaining Getting Around Changes (1).png|thumb|500px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-04-01/pitri1.png here]!'']]

Once you've reached the total amount of charges required, you'll get an in-game notification informing you that you've unlocked the infinite version of the Perfected Quetzal, which you can get by showing the whistle to Pitri.

[[File:Remaining Getting Around Changes (2).png|thumb|500px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-04-01/pitri2.png here]!'']]

Now, let's dive right into the remaining updates from the poll...

===River Dougne Canoe Stations===
[[File:Remaining Getting Around Changes (3).png|thumb|450px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-01-08/canoe.jpg here]!'']]

To make your travels across Kandarin smoother, we've added a new canoe route along the River Dougne, similar to the one along the River Lum. You'll find 5 new canoe stations added, connecting key locations across Kandarin while keeping the system rooted in its original design:

* Near Castle Wars:  Links up with the Ring of dueling and Balloon Network, and should be handy for Clue Scrolls.
* West of Tree Gnome Village: Close to the Farming patch and Spirit Tree.
* South of Ardougne Zoo: Provides easier access to central Ardougne, and also close to the Spirit Tree.
* East of Chaos Druid Tower: Improves travel to the Fishing Guild and North Ardougne.
* North of Combat Training Camp: Connects to Tree Gnome Village and Barbarian Assault.

[[File:Remaining Getting Around Changes (4).png|thumb|350px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-04-01/maps.png here]!'']]

For consistency, the River Lum canoe station interface has been updated to match that of the River Dougne.

[[File:Remaining Getting Around Changes (5).png|thumb|350px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-04-01/lum.png here]!'']]

Plus, you can now store and withdraw an axe at any canoe station along both the River Lum and River Dougne. Stored axes are shared across all stations, so once you’ve stored one, you’ll never have to worry about bringing an axe to use canoes again. You'll also find that you don't need to withdraw the axe to use it - just interact with the tree and you're good to go!

[[File:Remaining Getting Around Changes (6).png|thumb|350px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-04-01/axe.png here]!'']]

Note that existing canoe types and level requirements also apply to the River Dougne canoe stations.

===Faster Agility Shortcuts===
We feel that some Agility shortcuts can do with a bit of trimming to ''really'' feel like shortcuts. For this reason, we've made the following changes:

* Stepping stone shortcuts now require just a single click to cross, rather than having to click each stone.
* Animations for certain Agility shortcuts have been shortened where they previously felt too long, so you’ll spend less time watching your character shuffle about.
* Unnecessary delays have been removed. For example, your character won’t be left standing around before crossing.

We've made these changes the below shortcuts:

* Draynor to Port Sarim tunnel
* Falador crumbled wall
* Rocks north-west of Corsair Cove
* Kalphite Queen entrance
* Falador fence jump
* Dwarven Mine crevice
* Alchemical Hydra shortcut

No more awkward pauses and unnecessary clicks at certain shortcuts, making them feel more worthwhile once you've unlocked them.

===Fairy Ring Favourites===
Previously, even if you've favourited destinations on a Fairy ring, you had to go through the Configure option first. With this change, we've removed a few unnecessary clicks and reduced the menu navigation for players who know where they’re going.

[[File:Remaining Getting Around Changes (7).png|thumb|450px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-04-01/favourite.png here]!'']]

You'll now see a new 'Favourites' right-click option added to Fairy rings, if you have at least one destination marked as favourite. Hovering over this option will display a sub-menu of your favourite destinations, allowing you to teleport immediately with a single click! If you don't see this option at Fairy rings, it just means you haven't saved any favourites yet.

===Last Destination option to Spirit Trees===
To make Spirit Tree travels more convenient for those who regularly bounce between the same locations, we've added a 'Last Destination' option to them. Right-clicking a Spirit Tree and selecting this option will teleport you straight to the last location you travelled to using any Spirit Tree, without needing to open the full destination menu.

[[File:Remaining Getting Around Changes (8).png|thumb|400px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-04-01/lastdestination.png here]!'']]

* The Last Destination is shared across all Spirit Trees.
* If you haven’t travelled using a Spirit Tree yet, you’ll be told there’s no destination to return to.
* If you’re already at your last destination, the game will let you know instead of teleporting you.
* This option is available on all Spirit Trees except Spiritual Fairy Tree in the Player-Owned houses. In the POH, Spirit Trees share menu space with Fairy rings, leaving no room for the Last Destination option to be added.

===Lunar Return Orb===
In a similar vein, we've made a small tweak to the Lunar return orb.

We've added a toggle to the Lunar return orb so you can choose whether it immediately teleports you on left-click. You can access this toggle by using the new right-click 'Ponder' option on the Return orb.

[[File:Remaining Getting Around Changes (9).png|thumb|400px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-03-31/ponder.png here]!'']]


[[File:Remaining Getting Around Changes (10).png|thumb|500px|center|''You can enable the toggle by choosing the "Yes, and don't ask again" option.
If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-03-31/orb.png here]!'']]

* When the toggle is enabled, left-clicking the Return Orb will teleport you to Rellekka immediately, without opening a  confirmation dialogue. This will offer a quicker option for those who frequently use the orb.
* When the toggle is disabled, the Return Orb will behave exactly as it has always did, showing the confirmation dialogue before teleporting, for safeguard reasons.
* The toggle is enabled by default, but can be switched off at any time, maintaining the previous behaviour available for players who prefer the extra confirmation.

And that's a wrap for the Getting Around Poll changes! Now that all of them have made their way into the game, we hope these changes make your journeys across Gielinor smoother and snappier. More convenience, less clicks!

==Boat Combat Tweaks==
Following your feedback, we've got further boat combat balancing changes, as we mentioned <u>[https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/a=13/easter-2026--pvp-qol-improvements?oldschool=1#Sailing last week]</u>. We'll be closely monitoring how these changes feel in practice, so let us know your thoughts on our usual social channels.

===Buff to Cannons Manned by Player===
To start with, we've applied a buff to cannonballs and cannons when they are actively ''manned by a player''.  Our goal here was to close the gap between cannons and player gear, ensuring that a player using a cannon is on par to the DPS of traditional combat +2 Crew members using cannons.

You can expect max hits like in the below video while you man the Dragon Cannon.
[[File:Remaining Getting Around Changes (11).mp4|thumb|600px|center|''If you can’t see the asset above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-03-25/videowip.mp4 here]!'']]

To clarify further, cannons and cannonballs now have new stats applied to them called Heavy Ranged Accuracy and Heavy Ranged Strength. These work as you expect - they add bonuses to your Heavy Ranged combat with cannons, on top of the existing stats. However, crewmates do not benefit from these new stats.

